  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project Output/s</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output/s as listed by the project staff.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1  Indicator 4</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: Output 1 
Indicator: Capacity of executing and implementing agencies, and implementation arrangements are tested. 
Progress/Status: SMEC capacity assessment report submitted in November 2023. The report identified weakness in project management and technical capacity, including financial management. Through the PRF, an IFMS was engaged, and the PRF consultant who provide implementation and management support to the DTC&amp;I PMU. The PRF will also provide project auditing support once the recruitment of the consultant is completed.</narrative>
    </description>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1  Indicator 2</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: Output 1 
Indicator: Detailed engineering designs and bidding documents prepared, implementation contracts procured. 
Progress/Status: The draft detailed designs, bid documents, bill of quantities, cost analysis, and the initial draft due diligence outputs including the strategic procurement plan (SPP)(output 3) for the shortlisted priority roads and the Yap bridge, as envisaged under outputs 1, 2, and 4 were submitted in November 2023. ADB comments on the drafts were provided for most draft reports while others still being reviewed. SPP and procurement plan have been finalized. Bidding documents for the 5 civil works packages have been posted on 26 April 2026.</narrative>
    </description>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1  Indicator 3</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: Output 1 
Indicator: Innovative tools for road rehabilitation works in the FSM piloted. 
Progress/Status: Procurement of FDR machine and IC equipment, related civil works, and PMU office equipment are ongoing. DTC&amp;I submitted the summary evaluation report to ADB in Dec 2023. Following ADB and PMU follow-on discussion in early January 2024, the DTC&amp;I will submit additional information to substantiate their reasons for award of contracts as recommended. Contracts for the FDR equipment (US$747,264.00) and civil works for pilot test (US$384,253.62) have been awarded in May 2024. Pilot works due to commence in November 2024.</narrative>
    </description>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1  Indicator 1</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output: Output 1 
Indicator: Scope of sector policies, strategies, and investments identified. 
Progress/Status: Contract for the PRF Consultant for Project Prioritization, Readiness, and Pilot-testing (CS1) was awarded in July 2022. Road sector analysis report was submitted in April 2023. Summary Road Sector Assessment report was submitted on 20 December 2023. Due diligence report were completed in June 2024.</narrative>
    </description>
   </indicator>
